            <ArticleTitle>Heterotopic pregnancy presenting at 18 weeks' gestational age: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>748-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Heterotopic pregnancy is a rare event that usually presents in the first 6-8 weeks of pregnancy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 35-year-old primigravida was referred to the hospital at 18+ weeks' gestational age for evaluation of chronic abdominal pain. Ultrasound revealed a heterotopic pregnancy. The patient underwent surgery for removal of the ectopic pregnancy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Heterotopic pregnancy can present at any time during pregnancy and should be considered in any pregnant woman with abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
